WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:08.390
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:14.890
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.730
It's my day!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.310
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.710
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:42.090
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:49.490
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.270
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:02.410
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.910
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.050
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.120
I just want to walk

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.660
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.630
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:35.540
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:41.980
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.250
It's my day!

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:51.160
We've got to squish the bug quickly...

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.360
before the Domyoji name
comes to further harm.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.430
I thought it might be a little early...

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.130
But let us proceed
with the plan immediately.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.150
Are you referring to the plan
you were saving...

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.310
for after Tsukasa's graduation
from college?

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.440
Don't make me repeat myself, Nishida.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.280
The fate of the Domyoji Zaibatsu
is at stake.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:18.980
I won't let it be left at the mercy
of Tsukasa's whim.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:28.460
"Tsukasa's Mother's Secret Plan"

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.470
I'm hungry.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.000
You're scary, too!
Why the angry face?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.770
I get irritable when I'm hungry.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.280
<i>What a baby!</i>

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.780
So let's just go home.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:48.580
No way.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.280
Don't be childish!

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:56.020
Whoa...

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:02.560
There wasn't time to eat anything
at the party.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.000
We've got enough liquor
to fill a bathtub, but...

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:07.700
Oh!

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.500
Hey, we can go fishing!

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:16.010
I think the rods Kazuya and I used
in Atami should be here.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:17.680
Fishing?

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.010
Let's do it!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.400
Long ago, when my Grandma
used to live by the sea,

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.990
we used to go clamming.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.060
Climbing?

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.730
Clamming!
Don't you know what that is?

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.660
You use a little rake
to dig up clams in the sand.

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:44.640
You have to bend over like this
to search for the clams.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.040
One day, my dad overdid it and
threw out his back.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.310
We all had to carry him home.
What a mess...

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.020
Your family's interesting.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.150
Really?
We're just an average family.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.610
You're <i>so</i> poor, and have a
good-for-nothing dad

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.420
and live in a home the size
of our bathroom...

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.360
I wouldn't be caught dead
living like that.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:11.630
I'm gonna hit you.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.130
But it seems like fun.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.970
<i>Ah... I see...</i>

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:24.780
<i>Tsukasa lived with just his sister
since he was little.</i>

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.350
<i>And his mother is so overbearing...</i>

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.220
<i>There's no telling
what makes people happy.</i>

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.150
Oh, no... Have you caught a cold?

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.960
I borrowed your jacket earlier.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.170
I'm fine.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.800
Here. Let's share this.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:50.800
It's okay.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.440
It's not okay.
I don't want you blaming me.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:55.510
Here!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.450
<i>Oh...</i>

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:03.610
<i>His arm...</i>

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.460
H-hey... Don't come too close.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.730
What do you mean?
You moved over.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.860
But your arm's touching mine.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.300
W-what... what is it?

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.090
If you get all stiff like that,
I can't do anything that I'd like to do...

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.840
D-do anything?

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.880
What are you talking about?

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.240
Try anything funny,
and I'll push you overboard.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.910
Well, I'm in love with you,
you know.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:37.220
There's all sorts of things
I'd like to do.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.120
<i>All sorts of things?!</i>

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.860
Well, there's nothing
I want to do. At all.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.320
You're a weird girl.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:48.990
If a guy and a girl are in love,
it all comes naturally.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.360
Of course, there are
unprincipled guys like Sojiro.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.370
In love?!

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.030
Listen here...

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:59.900
Aren't you fooling yourself here?

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:05.880
'Cause I've been wondering...
What makes you think I love you?

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:06.880
It just hit me.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:09.210
Hit you?

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.550
Listen, you can't just go
making assumptions.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:19.960
Am I wrong? Let's settle this,
once and for all.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.060
How do you feel about me?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.000
How do I feel?

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.430
I'm not sure.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.710
You're always like that.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.480
But I really don't know.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.310
I'm not trying to tease you
or be mean to you.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:56.090
You'll catch a cold. Sit.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:09.010
Domyoji...
I've been wanting to ask you...

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.280
Why me?

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.720
I haven't got status, or prestige,
or beauty...

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:26.560
There are lots of girls at Eitoku
who have all three.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:33.430
I just can't figure out why it's me...

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.600
The only explanation I can think of
is that you're crazy.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:38.500
Maybe I am.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.510
I wonder why myself...

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:45.310
But this is something
you just can't reason out.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:50.550
Besides, I've got the status,
prestige, and beauty...

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.950
so you can stay as you are.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.120
Beauty?
What do you mean, beauty?

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.660
I'll admit you have
the status and prestige...

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.390
You idiot...

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.260
If there is anyone
with all three attributes...

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.500
I'd like to meet her.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:13.240
<i>Good grief...</i>

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.440
<i>Where does all that confidence
come from?</i>

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:22.430
<i>He thinks it's inevitable
that I would fall in love with him.</i>

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.770
Wow! It's a big one.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.850
Put your back into it!

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:29.020
<i>If I'm not careful,
I might get sucked in.</i>

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:35.590
<i>It's like this night sea,
where you can't see the horizon.</i>

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.570
What's big about this?

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.970
It's a HUGE... bunch of kelp.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.280
It's seaweed!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:58.350
I'm starving.
What a waste of energy!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.750
Don't exaggerate!

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:04.440
Unlike you,
I don't have much body fat,

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.220
so lack of food hits me harder.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.460
Cold <i>and</i> hungry...

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:14.000
They say that people resort to death
if they're sleepy on top of that.

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.140
<i>I can't show him this...</i>

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:28.350
What is that?

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.550
Uh... it's nothing.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.690
You're hiding something.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.690
No, I'm not.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:38.190
Show it to me!

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:40.090
No! No!

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.660
No!

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:47.630
What's this?

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.470
Your birthday present.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:56.740
Present? You said you forgot it.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:02.010
Well... the other presents were so grand...
Like that car...

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.450
I couldn't give this to you.

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:10.560
<i>Oh... It took me an hour to wrap it!</i>

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:20.600
<i>He'll probably make fun of it...
Calling it lame... Oh, I hate this...</i>

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.470
We don't have an oven...

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:41.290
so I used a fish grill, and
they got burnt.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.920
Actually, they might smell like fish...

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:52.660
Hey! Don't stare at them like that.
It's embarrassing.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:58.440
Sorry it's so lame.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.070
It's all I could afford.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.330
It was easy to get your face right,
with your distinct features...

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:04.840
...but your hair was a lot tougher.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.620
Come on...!
Just give them back to me!

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.810
I'm <i>so</i> happy!

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:42.310
<i>I'd never seen that
childish look of delight on his face...</i>

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:47.090
<i>I forgot to be angry with him.</i>

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.710
<i>I never thought Domyoji
would be so happy...</i>

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:14.010
<i>with my cheap homemade cookies.</i>

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:19.920
Thanks for lending me your jacket.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.390
What are you going to do...
go home?

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:29.090
How can I? I'll just hide out
'til my mother leaves for New York.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:31.400
I see...

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:32.730
See you later...

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:35.430
Hey, Makino...

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:36.130
Huh?

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:43.810
I LOVE YOU

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.480
<i>What?</i>

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:53.150
<i>What was that?</i>

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:09.530
<i>I'm so tired...</i>

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.700
<i>I wonder if it's
from all that tension.</i>

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:16.070
<i>It's been such a long day.</i>

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:21.980
<i>That guy...</i>

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.020
<i>I was just as bad.</i>

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:29.990
<i>Why couldn't I have
slapped his face?!</i>

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:35.190
<i>I'm so happy!</i>

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.960
<i>I'm hungry too.</i>

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:41.190
<i>You gave this to me.</i>

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:42.770
<i>You made them,
so you can't eat them!</i>

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.740
<i>What ugly cookies!
I'll bet they taste bad.</i>

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:54.350
<i>He didn't even eat them.
Just stared at them.</i>

00:13:56.310 --> 00:14:00.550
<i>What could he have been thinking?
Does he love cookies that much?</i>

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:10.430
<i>He... loves me...</i>

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:20.670
<i>What am I going to do?</i>

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:27.380
<i>I guess I'll get some sleep.</i>

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:30.880
<i>I must be getting old...</i>

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:44.900
Yo!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:50.270
How long are you going to sleep?
Get up, will you?

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:52.940
I'm gonna open the window.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.890
Your room is as empty as ever.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.280
At least put a couch in here
for your guests.

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:02.610
What's up?

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:04.880
What do you mean?!

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.620
Your friend is visiting.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.220
A visit?

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.730
It's only 6:30 in the morning.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:18.460
It's too beautiful a morning to sleep in.
You'll get moldy.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.970
Did something good happen?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.840
N-no, of course not.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.470
Hey! Don't go back to sleep,
you sleepyhead!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.750
I went out on the cruiser and
did some fishing.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:36.980
Cool, huh? Sounds fun, huh?

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:39.820
But there was nothing to eat.
And then...

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:41.020
Look...

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:45.790
It's my present.
She baked them for me.

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:54.270
She keeps pushing me away, but
I think she really likes me.

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:57.770
People don't usually give
homemade things...

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:02.010
Well, homemade stuff
kinda grosses me out...

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:06.140
Can you tell who this is?
It's me... Me!

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:07.750
That's great.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:11.620
Hey! Don't eat it, you!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:15.220
I haven't even had one.
Spit it out! Spit it out!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.220
It smells like fish...

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.640
Hasn't Tsukasa come home yet?

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.100
No. Not yet.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:38.740
That fool! To keep a young girl
out until morning...

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:42.750
It's an emergency situation!
Where could he be?

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:45.280
What's this emergency situation?

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.820
Good morning, Madam...

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:53.360
How old do you think
you are, Tsubaki?

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.100
It's unbecoming for you to be
making such a fuss.

00:16:57.730 --> 00:17:00.260
Is that how a married woman
should act?

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.330
You should be ashamed
of yourself.

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:07.040
I'll just have some fruit
and an espresso.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.380
Then bring me the annual reports.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.040
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:16.610
I'll be going out soon. Have the chauffer
prepare the car for me.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:17.520
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:31.600
Mother... When will you
be returning to New York?

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:35.570
You usually leave
the day after his birthday.

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:40.740
There are some things
I have to take care of...

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.070
I'll leave after that.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:47.380
Things you have to take care of?

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.500
What are you doing to do
to Tsukasa and Tsukushi?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.650
Don't tell me you'll be
as cruel as you were to me!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.450
Tsubaki! Watch your mouth!

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:02.930
Who do you think you owe for your happy,
wonderful life, free from want?

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:05.730
I've had enough
of your ridiculous complaints.

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.170
But... There were things that I lost.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:15.310
Those things... were not important.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:55.080
You'll never understand... Never...

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.990
Who could it be,
so early in the morning?

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:03.620
Get the door, will you dear?

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:05.760
Okay...

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:09.930
No salespeople allowed!

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.730
We don't even take the newspaper!

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:15.670
Is this the home of Tsukushi Makino?

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.540
Tsukushi! Wake up!

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:21.270
Tsukushi!

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:25.840
What are you doing...
catching seaweed?

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:32.480
Tsukushi! Mrs. Domyoji is here!
Get up, will you!

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:47.300
I'm h-happy to m-m-meet...
I'm Tsukushi's mother...

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:50.840
<i>You're my father!</i>

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:54.670
I am Tsukasa's mother.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.840
Pardon me for calling on you
so early in the morning.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:01.450
Your son has been
very kind to Tsukushi...

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:06.250
<i>Mom and Dad are so tense...
I don't blame them.</i>

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:12.390
<i>No one could remain calm
in the presence of this woman.</i>

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:15.090
Nishida, if you will...

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.730
I will be blunt.

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:23.630
I want Tsukushi to give Tsukasa up.

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:26.800
I'm willing to give her an incentive.

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:30.980
There's 50 million yen here.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:36.110
F-fifty million yen?!

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:42.970
I'm sorry, but I noticed that you seem
to be short on funds,

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:44.560
so I had this prepared for you.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:49.760
As you know, Tsukasa has
a great future before him.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:55.430
He's reached the 
age where he must be careful 
to avoid even the tiniest of pebbles.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:02.070
<i>Wait a minute!
Is she calling me a pebble?</i>

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:08.050
<i>And she wants me to stay away
from Domyoji for 50 million yen?</i>

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:13.220
<i>What a laugh! It's him
who's been chasing after me!</i>

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:17.960
<i>She checked up on us and decided
we'd gladly take the money...</i>

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:21.860
<i>This old hag!
How rude can she be?!</i>

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.260
<i>I can't stand this!</i>

00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:30.740
SALT

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:52.360
Take your money... and get out!

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:54.060
<i>Mom?!</i>

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:04.940
Will I ever make it that far?

00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:09.710
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:22:11.510 --> 00:22:19.150
Some day, the whole world

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:24.960
will have its eyes on me.

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:32.730
Yeah, after our graduation ceremony

00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:38.340
we all wrote our dreams on the wall.

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:44.980
A lot of time has passed since then

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:51.350
but I'm just the same as I was on that day!

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:58.260
Keep trying your best! 
Wishes can come true!

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:07.130
Let's keep running down
 the road we believe in!

00:23:08.430 --> 00:23:15.040
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:21.110
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:28.390
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:31.760
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:37.630
I already made it this far, after all.

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:48.010
How dare she!

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:52.010
The rich think they can get anyone
to do anything for money!

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:56.250
I'm gonna tell her...
We don't live in the same world.

00:23:57.320 --> 00:23:59.750
He'll probably wake up
to that fact, too.

00:24:00.520 --> 00:24:03.190
Hana Yori Dango:
"It's Showdown Time!"

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:08.430
I have a bad feeling
about that fleeting smile...
